-- title:
--   Theorem 3.2 — tangent-residual bound for AEP
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be continuous and monotone, let $H$ be maximal monotone, let $z^\ast$ be any solution of Problem (1), and let $\rho\in[0,1]$. Along any run of the AEP framework (Algorithm 2) with anchor $z_0$, for every update $k$,
--   $$
--   v_{k+1}\in H(z_{k+1})\qquad\text{and}\qquad \mathrm{res}^{\tan}(z_{k+1})\le\|F(z_{k+1})+v_{k+1}\|\le\frac{2\|z_0-z^\ast\|}{A_{k+1}} .
--   $$
--   Inexact proximal steps satisfying the relative-error condition thus retain the guarantee of the exact anchored proximal point method: the tangent residual decays like the inverse of the cumulative step size.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: {z_k} generated by AEP in Algorithm 2, for every k ≥ 0 → sequences with IsAEPRun F H ρ z zh v r a A K (anchor z 0), claim for every update k < K; reason: the stopping test only truncates a run; K is arbitrary, so every finite or infinite run is covered
--   - encoding: res^tan(z) = inf over H(z) of ‖F(z)+v‖ (+∞ on an empty set) → tangentResidual = real sInf of the image (0 on an empty set); reason: the same value whenever H(z) is nonempty, which the stated membership guarantees
--   - generalization: res^tan(z_{k+1}) ≤ ‖F(z_{k+1}) + v_{k+1}‖ ≤ 2‖z₀ − z∗‖/A_{k+1} → additionally v_{k+1} ∈ H(z_{k+1}); reason: the membership is noted in the source after (13); stating it makes the bound a certificate
-- source:
--   Jiang–Yoon, Anchored Extra-Proximal Methods: Optimal Higher-Order Methods for Monotone Inclusion Problems, arXiv:2609.30212, Theorem 3.2, p.6

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ThreeOpSplitting_Convergence_MonotoneOperators
import Definitions.Def_AnchoredEP_IsSolution
import Definitions.Def_AnchoredEP_tangentResidual
import Definitions.Def_AnchoredEP_IsAEPRun

open ThreeOpSplitting.Convergence

namespace AnchoredEP

/-- **Theorem 3.2 (tangent-residual bound for AEP).** Jiang–Yoon, arXiv:2609.30212, Theorem 3.2,
p.6: "Let `{z_k}_{k≥0}` be generated by AEP in Algorithm 2 with `ρ ∈ [0, 1]`. Then, for every
`k ≥ 0`, `res^tan(z_{k+1}) ≤ ‖F(z_{k+1}) + v_{k+1}‖ ≤ 2‖z₀ − z∗‖/A_{k+1}`."

Standing assumptions (p.1): `F` continuous and monotone, `H` maximal monotone, `z∗` a solution of
Problem (1) (any solution).

**Formalization Note.** The run is `IsAEPRun … K` with anchor `z₀ = z 0`; the bound is asserted
for every update `k < K` performed. Besides the source's chain of inequalities the statement
records `v_{k+1} ∈ H(z_{k+1})`, which makes the bound a certificate (the real `sInf` in
`tangentResidual` would be `0` on an empty `H(z_{k+1})`). `A_{k+1} > 0` because `a_k > 0`. -/
theorem theorem_3_2 {d : ℕ} (F : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d) → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d))
    (H : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d) → Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d)))
    (hFc : Continuous F)
    (hF : IsMonotoneOp (fun x => ({F x} : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d)))))
    (hH : IsMaximalMonotone H)
    (zstar : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d)) (hstar : IsSolution F H zstar)
    (ρ : ℝ) (hρ0 : 0 ≤ ρ) (hρ1 : ρ ≤ 1)
    (z zh v r : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d)) (a A : ℕ → ℝ) (K : ℕ)
    (hrun : IsAEPRun F H ρ z zh v r a A K) :
    ∀ k < K, v (k + 1) ∈ H (z (k + 1)) ∧
      tangentResidual F H (z (k + 1)) ≤ ‖F (z (k + 1)) + v (k + 1)‖ ∧
      ‖F (z (k + 1)) + v (k + 1)‖ ≤ 2 * ‖z 0 - zstar‖ / A (k + 1) := by sorry

end AnchoredEP
